tus":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-24T07:32:35Z","content":"# Resuming from a compaction\n\nYou are continuing work on the task described above, but you have lost access to the full conversation history, and need to resume work efficiently using the progress summary below:\n\n# User Requests\nThe following were user requests from the truncated conversation in chronological order:\n1. 请接收数据获取蛋返回的上海温度结构化数据，将其渲染为友好的卡片 UI，突出展示上海当前温度及未来3天温度趋势。\n\n<summary>\n## 1. Task Overview\n- **Core request (user, in Chinese):** As the \"展示蛋\" (e3) module, receive the structured Shanghai temperature data returned by the \"数据获取蛋\" (e2) and render it as a friendly card UI that highlights (a) Shanghai's current temperature and (b) the 3-day temperature trend.\n- **Success criteria:** A working card UI in the e3 workspace showing Shanghai's current temp prominently + a 3-day trend (high/low per day, visual trend indicator).\n- **Constraints:** Source files only under `/home/administator/workspace/create_idea/worktrees/e1/e3`; dependency-free plain Node; preserve backward compatibility with existing tests; concise GitHub-markdown response with file:// links.\n- **Ambiguity resolved:** No Shanghai data existed in e3, so the canonical source is sibling egg e2's `shanghai_weather.json`. The e2 schema differs from e3's card schema, so a mapping/normalization layer is required (not hand-editing sample.json, not hardcoding).\n\n## 2. Progress\n**Completed:**\n- Located and read e2 data: `/home/administator/workspace/create_idea/worktrees/e1/e2/shanghai_weather.json` (1428 B).\n- Copied it into e3: `/home/administator/workspace/create_idea/worktrees/e1/e3/data/shanghai.json` — **done successfully** (cp returned exit 0).\n- Explored all e3 files (read in full):\n  - `src/weather-card.js` (230 lines) — dependency-free. Exports: `renderWeatherCard`, `renderWeatherGrid`, `renderWeatherGridToElement`, `injectStyles`, `resolveCondition`, `unitOf`. Internals: `ICONS`, `GRADIENTS`, `KEYWORD_RULES`, `esc()`, `themeFor()`, `statRows()`, `hourlyRow()`, `CARD_CSS` template literal.\n  - `data/sample.json` — Tokyo/Reykjavík/Dubai (no Shanghai).\n  - `index.html` — ES module; imports `./src/weather-card.js` + `../data/sample.json`, renders into `#weather`.\n  - `test/weather-card.test.js` — plain Node assertion harness; run via `node test/weather-card.test.js`.\n  - `package.json` — name \"weather-card\", `\"type\": \"module\"`.\n- Node version confirmed: **v24.21.0**.\n\n**In progress / incomplete:**\n- Nothing has been written yet for the Shanghai card: no mapping layer, no daily/trend renderer, no index.html update, no new tests.\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n**e2 schema (real data shape to consume):**\n- `city: \"Shanghai\"`, `country: \"China\"`, `coordinates`, `timezone: \"Asia/Shanghai\"`, `source`.\n- `current_weather`: `{ observed_at: \"2026-10-24T15:15\", temperature_c: 20.7, feels_like_c: 21.6, humidity_pct: 87, wind_speed_mps: 15.2, precipitation_mm: 0.1, weather_code: 51 }`.\n- `daily_forecast`: 3 objects, each `{date, weather, weather_code, temp_max_c, temp_min_c, feels_like_max_c, feels_like_min_c, humidity_pct, wind_speed_max_mps, precip_prob_pct, precipitation_mm}`:\n  - 2026-10-24: 中阵雨, code 81, max 20.9 / min 18.1\n  - 2026-10-25: 毛毛雨, code 51, max 23.5 / min 17.9\n  - 2026-10-26: 少云, code 2, max 22.8 / min 16.5\n\n**e3 card schema (what `renderWeatherCard` expects):** `{city, country, temp, unit, condition/icon, description, humidity, windKmh, windDirection, high, low, time, hourly}`.\n\n**Conversion notes (for the mapper):**\n- `temp` ← `current_weather.temperature_c` (20.7); `feelsLike` ← `feels_like_c` (21.6); `humidity` ← `humidity_pct` (87).\n- `windKmh` ← `wind_speed_mps * 3.6` (15.2 → ~54.7 km/h).\n- `condition` ← map Open-Meteo `weather_code`: 51 → `drizzle`, 81 → `rain` (or `heavy-rain`), 2 → `partly-cloudy`. (Open-Meteo codes: 0 clear, 1–3 partly-cloudy, 4–6 overcast, 51–67 drizzle, 71–77 rain, 80–82 showers, 95 thunderstorm, 100+ snow.)\n- `time` ← extract HH:MM from `observed_at` → `\"15:15\"`.\n- `high`/`low` ← `daily_forecast[0].temp_max_c` / `temp_min_c` (20.9 / 18.1).\n- Pass through a `daily` array (3 entries) for the new trend renderer.\n\n**Feature to add:** a 3-day trend renderer (e.g. `dailyRow(daily, unit)` → `.wc-daily` block) with day label + high/low + a simple visual bar/arrow showing the trend. Add matching `.wc-daily` CSS into `CARD_CSS`. Include it in `renderWeatherCard`.\n\n**Approaches tried and abandoned:** None yet — no code written. The tempting-but-wrong approach is to hand-edit `data/sample.json` or hardcode Shanghai; instead, copy the real e2 JSON into `e3/data/shanghai.json` (already done) and map it.\n\n## 4. Active Context\n- No browser needed; module emits HTML strings; tests run in plain Node.\n- Environment: Linux, Node v24.21.0, `package.json` type: module.\n- Dependency chain: `index.html` → `src/weather-card.js` + `data/shanghai.json` (e2 data).\n- Working assumption: e2's `shanghai_weather.json` is the canonical source; copied into e3 to keep e3 self-contained and testable.\n\n## 5. Next Steps\n1. **Extend `src/weather-card.js`:**\n   - Add exported `mapShanghaiData(raw)` (or generic `normalizeCity(raw)`) converting the e2 schema → the card schema (see conversion notes), including a `daily` array of 3 entries.\n   - Add `dailyRow(daily, unit)` rendering the 3-day trend (day label, high/low, visual bar/arrow); append `.wc-daily` CSS to `CARD_CSS`; include in `renderWeatherCard`.\n   - Keep existing API backward-compatible.\n2. **Update `index.html`:** import `../data/shanghai.json`, map via the new function, render into `#weather`; title text like \"上海天气\".\n3. **Add tests** in `test/weather-card.test.js` for the 3-day trend (3 days present, high/low values present, correct day labels) and for the mapper (temp 20.7, humidity 87, time \"15:15\").\n4. **Run** `node test/weather-card.test.js` from e3; verify all pass.\n5. **Verify** the rendered UI (open/serve `index.html` or inspect the HTML string) and report the built UI concisely with file:// links.\n\n## 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Source files only under `/home/administator/workspace/create_idea/worktrees/e1/e3`.\n- Module stays dependency-free; tests must run with plain Node.\n- Existing tests must still pass after changes (backward compatibility required).\n- Response: concise, GitHub-markdown, file:// links to created/modified files.\n</summary>\n\n# Conversation Logs\nStart with the compact transcript; if a step has `truncated_fields`, read only that specific line in `transcript_full.jsonl`:\n- `<appDataDir>/brain/<conversation-id>/.system_generated/logs/transcript.jsonl`\n- `<appDataDir>/brain/<conversation-id>/.system_generated/logs/transcript_full.jsonl`"}
