.js` doc comment (lines ~6–29) to document new `mapShanghaiData` API and optional `daily` field in the `city` shape.\n- **Edit 2 done:** Inserted after `KEYWORD_RULES` (before `esc()`): `WMO_CODE_MAP` (Open-Meteo WMO codes → card codes, e.g. 51→'drizzle', 81→'rain', 2→'partly-cloudy'), `WMO_ZH` (Chinese labels: 51→'毛毛雨', 81→'中阵雨', 2→'少云'), `codeToCondition(code)`, `round1(n)`, `extractTime(observedAt)` (regex `/T(\\d{2}:\\d{2})/`), `WEEKDAY_ZH`, `weekdayOf(dateStr)`.\n\n**In progress / incomplete:**\n- `mapShanghaiData` export NOT yet written.\n- `dailyRow(daily, unit)` trend renderer NOT yet written; `.wc-daily` CSS NOT yet added to `CARD_CSS`; `renderWeatherCard` NOT yet updated to include it.\n- `index.html` NOT yet pointed at Shanghai data.\n- No new tests added yet.\n\n## 3. Key Findings\n**e2 schema (real data in `data/shanghai.json`):**\n- `city: \"Shanghai\"`, `country: \"China\"`, `timezone: \"Asia/Shanghai\"`, `source: \"Open-Meteo API\"`.\n- `current_weather`: `{ observed_at: \"2026-10-24T15:15\", temperature_c: 20.7, feels_like_c: 21.6, humidity_pct: 87, wind_speed_mps: 15.2, precipitation_mm: 0.1, weather_code: 51 }`.\n- `daily_forecast`: 3 entries:\n  - 2026-10-24: 中阵雨, code 81, max 20.9 / min 18.1\n  - 2026-10-25: 毛毛雨, code 51, max 23.5 / min 17.9\n  - 2026-10-26: 少云, code 2, max 22.8 / min 16.5\n\n**e3 card schema (what `renderWeatherCard` expects):** `{city, country, temp, unit, condition/icon, description, humidity, windKmh, windDirection, high, low, time, hourly}`.\n\n**Conversion (for `mapShanghaiData(raw)`):**\n- `temp` ← `temperature_c` (20.7); `feelsLike` ← `feels_like_c` (21.6); `humidity` ← `humidity_pct` (87).\n- `windKmh` ← `round1(wind_speed_mps * 3.6)` (15.2 → 54.7).\n- `condition` ← `codeToCondition(weather_code).code` (51 → 'drizzle'); `description` ← `WMO_ZH[weather_code]` (or raw Chinese text).\n- `time` ← `extractTime(observed_at)` → `\"15:15\"`.\n- `high`/`low` ← `daily_forecast[0].temp_max_c` / `temp_min_c` (20.9 / 18.1).\n- `daily` ← 3 entries: `{ date, label (今天/明天/weekday), condition: codeToCondition(weather_code)?.code, description: raw weather text, high, low }`.\n- Keep existing API backward-compatible (all current exports unchanged).\n\n**Existing `renderWeatherCard` structure:** header (city+country+time), main (icon+temp+condition), `statRows(city)`, `hourlyRow(...)` → returns one `<article class=\"wc\">`. `CARD_CSS` is a template literal at end of file; `injectStyles()` injects it (browser-only, safe in Node).\n\n## 4. Active Context\n- No browser needed; module emits HTML strings; tests run in plain Node.\n- Environment: Linux, Node v24.21.0, `package.json` `\"type\": \"module\"`.\n- Working assumption: e2's `shanghai_weather.json` is canonical; copied into e3 (`data/shanghai.json`) to keep e3 self-contained and testable.\n- Current file: `src/weather-card.js` is ~285 lines after 2 edits; `esc()` intact; `renderWeatherCard` and `CARD_CSS` unchanged.\n\n## 5. Next Steps\n1. **Add `export function mapShanghaiData(raw)`** to `src/weather-card.js` (after `hourlyRow`, before `renderWeatherCard`): convert e2 schema → card schema per conversion notes above, including `daily` array of 3 entries. Use WMO_ZH for description when available.\n2. **Add `dailyRow(daily, unit)`** (export or internal + used by card): renders `.wc-daily` block — for each day: day label, condition icon (via `resolveCondition`), high/low values, and a simple visual trend indicator (CSS bar scaled by temp and/or ▲/▼/→ arrow vs previous day's high). Append `.wc-daily` CSS to `CARD_CSS`. Include in `renderWeatherCard` (after stats, before/after hourly).\n3. **Update `index.html`:** import `../data/shanghai.json` + `mapShanghaiData`; `renderWeatherGridToElement(document.getElementById('weather'), [mapShanghaiData(shanghai)]);`; title text like \"上海天气\" (hero h1/p).\n4. **Add tests** in `test/weather-card.test.js`: mapper (temp 20.7, humidity 87, time \"15:15\", condition 'drizzle', windKmh 54.7, daily length 3 with correct high/low), daily row (3 days present, high/low values, day labels).\n5. **Run** `node test/weather-card.test.js` from e3; verify all pass.\n6. **Verify** rendered HTML string (e.g., quick node script printing `renderWeatherCard(mapShanghaiData(shanghai))`) and report concisely with file:// links.\n\n## 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Source files only under `/home/administator/workspace/create_idea/worktrees/e1/e3`.\n- Module stays dependency-free; tests must run with plain Node.\n- Existing tests must still pass after changes (backward compatibility required).\n- Response: concise, GitHub-markdown, file:// links to created/modified files.\n- Do NOT hand-edit `data/sample.json` or hardcode Shanghai data — use the mapping layer over the real e2 JSON.\n\n</summary>\n\n# Conversation Logs\nStart with the compact transcript; if a step has `truncated_fields`, read only that specific line in `transcript_fu\n---\nThe checkpoint summary has been truncated due to hitting max length. Please see the conversation log file for the full conversation."}
