ta(raw)`:**\n- `city` ← `raw.city` (\"Shanghai\"); `country` ← `raw.country`.\n- `temp` ← `current_weather.temperature_c` (20.7); `feelsLike` ← `feels_like_c` (21.6); `humidity` ← `humidity_pct` (87).\n- `windKmh` ← `round1(wind_speed_mps * 3.6)` (15.2 → 54.7).\n- `condition` ← `codeToCondition(weather_code)?.code` (51 → 'drizzle'); `description` ← `WMO_ZH[weather_code]` (51 → '毛毛雨').\n- `time` ← `extractTime(observed_at)` → \"15:15\".\n- `high`/`low` ← `daily_forecast[0].temp_max_c` / `temp_min_c` (20.9 / 18.1).\n- `daily` ← 3 entries: `{ date, label (今天/明天/weekday via weekdayOf), condition: codeToCondition(code)?.code, description: raw weather text, high, low }`.\n- Keep existing exports unchanged (backward compatibility).\n\n**Existing `renderWeatherCard` structure:** header (city+country+time), main (icon+temp+condition), `statRows(city)`, `hourlyRow(...)` → returns one `<article class=\"wc\">`. `CARD_CSS` is a template literal at end of file (const hoisting is safe since `injectStyles()` only reads it at runtime).\n\n## 4. Active Context\n- No browser needed; module emits HTML strings; tests run in plain Node (v24.21.0, `package.json` `\"type\": \"module\"`).\n- Working assumption: e2's `shanghai_weather.json` is canonical; copied into e3 (`data/shanghai.json`) to keep e3 self-contained and testable.\n- `weekdayOf` uses `new Date(y, m-1, d)` — for 2026-10-24 that's a Friday (五); 2026-10-25 Saturday (六); 2026-10-26 Sunday (日). Labels: today = 今天, tomorrow = 明天, else weekday char.\n- Dependencies: `mapShanghaiData` depends on `codeToCondition`/`WMO_ZH`/`weekdayOf` (all written). `dailyRow` depends on `resolveCondition` (written).\n\n## 5. Next Steps\n1. **Fix `esc()` bug:** insert `function esc(v) {` before line 128 in `src/weather-card.js`.\n2. **Add `export function mapShanghaiData(raw)`** after `hourlyRow` (line 183), before `renderWeatherCard` (line 185), per conversion spec.\n3. **Add `dailyRow(daily, unit)`** (internal function, used by card): renders `.wc-daily` block — for each day: label, condition icon (via `resolveCondition`), high/low, and a visual trend indicator (▲/▼/→ arrow vs previous day's high, plus a CSS bar scaled by temp). Append `.wc-daily` CSS to `CARD_CSS`.\n4. **Update `renderWeatherCard`:** insert `dailyHtml = dailyRow(city.daily, unit)` after stats, before hourly.\n5. **Update `index.html`:** import `../data/shanghai.json` + `mapShanghaiData`; call `renderWeatherGridToElement(document.getElementById('weather'), [mapShanghaiData(shanghai)])`; change title/hero text to 上海天气.\n6. **Add tests** in `test/weather-card.test.js`: mapper (temp 20.7, humidity 87, time \"15:15\", condition 'drizzle', windKmh 54.7, daily length 3 with correct high/low), daily row (3 days present, high/low values, day labels).\n7. **Run** `node test/weather-card.test.js` from e3; verify all pass.\n8. **Verify** rendered HTML via quick node scrip\n---\nThe checkpoint summary has been truncated due to hitting max length. Please see the conversation log file for the full conversation."}
{"step_index":58,"source":"MODEL","type":"VIEW_FILE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-10-24T07:43:57Z","content":"Created At: 2026-10-24T15:43:57+08:00\nCompleted At: 2026-10-24T15:43:57+08:00\nFile Path: `file:///home/administator/workspace/create_idea/worktrees/e1/e3/src/weather-card.js`\nTotal Lines: 283\nTotal Bytes: 11842\nShowing lines 1 to 283\nThe following code has been modified to include a line number before every line, in the format: <line_number>: <original_line>. Please note that any changes targeting the original code should remove the line number, colon, and leading space.\n1: /**\n2:  * weather-card.js — dependency-free module that renders weather data into\n3:  * a friendly card UI.\n4:  *\n5:  * Public API\n6:  * ----------\n7:  *  renderWeatherCard(city)              -> string   (HTML for one card)\n8:  *  renderWeatherGrid(cities)            -> string   (HTML for a grid of cards)\n9:  *  renderWeatherGridToElement(el, cities) -> Element|null\n10:  *  injectStyles()                       -> void     (injects the card CSS, browser only)\n11:  *\n12:  *  Data normalization (data-fetching egg → card schema)\n13:  *  ---------------------------------------------------\n14:  *  mapShanghaiData(raw)                 -> object  (Open-Meteo-style raw data → card object,\n15:  *                                                   includes a `daily` array for the 3-day trend)\n16:  *\n17:  *  `city` shape (missing fields are gracefully omitted):\n18:  *   {\n19:  *     city: 'Tokyo',                     // required\n20:  *     country: 'JP',                     // optional\n21:  *     temp: 22,                          // required\n22:  *     unit: '°C',                        // optional ('C' | 'F' | '°C' | '°F'), default '°C'\n23:  *     feelsLike: 20,                     // optional\n24:  *     condition: 'partly-cloudy',        // code, icon name, or free text ('light rain'…)\n25:  *     icon: 'cloudy',                    // alternative to `condition`\n26:  *     description: 'Mostly sunny',       // optional human-readable description\n27:  *     humidity: 65,                      // optional, %\n28:  *     windKmh: 12,                       // optional\n29:  *     windDirection: 'NW',               // optional\n30:  *     high: 25, low: 17,                 // optional\n31:  *     time: '14:18',                     // optional display time\n32:  *     hourly: [{ time: '15:00', temp: 22, condition: 'cloudy' }]\n33:  *     daily:  [{ date, label, condition, description, high, low }]   // optional, 3-day trend\n34:  *   }\n35:  */\n36: \n37: const ICONS = {\n38:   clear:           { emoji: '☀️', label: 'Sunny' },\n39:   'clear-night':   { emoji: '🌙', label: 'Clear night' },\n40:   'partly-cloudy': { emoji: '🌤️', label: 'Partly cloudy' },\n41:   cloudy:          { emoji: '☁️', label: 'Cloudy' },\n42:   overcast:        { emoji: '☁️', label: 'Overcast' },\n43:   fog:             { emoji: '🌫️', label: 'Foggy' },\n44:   drizzle:         { emoji: '🌦️', label: 'Drizzle' },\n45:   rain:            { emoji: '🌧️', label: 'Rainy' },\n46:   'heavy-rain':    { emoji: '🌧️', label: 'Heavy rain' },\n47:   thunderstorm:    { emoji: '⛈️', label: 'Thunderstorm' },\n48:   snow:            { emoji: '❄️', label: 'Snowy' },\n49:   sleet:           { emoji: '🌨️', label: 'Sleet' },\n50: };\n51: \n52: const GRADIENTS = {\n53:   clear:           'linear-gradient(135deg, #ffd166, #f77f00)',\n54:   'clear-night':   'linear-gradient(135deg, #1e3a5f, #0d1b2a)',\n55:   'partly-cloudy': 'linear-gradient(135deg, #90caf9, #4fc3f7)',\n56:   cloudy:          'linear-gradient(135deg, #b0bec5, #78909c)',\n57:   overcast:        'linear-gradient(135deg, #90a4ae, #546e7a)',\n58:   fog:             'linear-gradient(135deg, #eceff1, #b0bec5)',\n59:   drizzle:         'linear-gradient(135deg, #78909c, #546e7a)',\n60:   rain:            'linear-gradient(135deg, #546e7a, #263238)',\n61:   'heavy-rain':    'linear-gradient(135deg, #37474f, #1a2228)',\n62:   thunderstorm:    'linear-gradient(135deg, #455a64, #1a2228)',\n63:   snow:            'linear-gradient(135deg, #e0f7fa, #b2dfdb)',\n64:   sleet:           'linear-gradient(135deg, #cfd8dc, #90a4ae)',\n65: };\n66: \n67: const LIGHT = ['clear', 'partly-cloudy', 'cloudy', 'overcast', 'fog', 'drizzle', 'snow', 'sleet'];\n68: \n69: const FALLBACK = { emoji: '☁️', label: 'Weather' };\n70: \n71: const KEYWORD_RULES = [\n72:   { re: /thunder|lightning|storm/, name: { code: 'thunderstorm', emoji: '⛈️', label: 'Thunderstorm' } },\n73:   { re: /snow|sleet/,              name: { code: 'snow', ...ICONS.snow } },\n74:   { re: /rain|drizzle/,           name: { code: 'rain', ...ICONS.rain } },\n75:   { re: /fog|mist|haze/,          name: { code: 'fog', ...ICONS.fog } },\n76:   { re: /cloud|overcast/,         name: { code: 'cloudy', ...ICONS.cloudy } },\n77:   { re: /clear|sunny|sun/,        name: { code: 'clear', ...ICONS.clear } },\n78: ];\n79: \n80: /**\n81:  * Open-Meteo WMO weather codes → card condition codes, used to normalize\n82:  * the structured data returned by the data-fetching egg.\n83:  */\n84: const WMO_CODE_MAP = {\n85:   0: 'clear', 1: 'partly-cloudy', 2: 'partly-cloudy', 3: 'overcast',\n86:   45: 'fog', 48: 'fog',\n87:   51: 'drizzle', 53: 'drizzle', 55: 'drizzle',\n88:   56: 'sleet', 57: 'sleet',\n89:   61: 'rain', 63: 'rain', 65: 'rain',\n90:   66: 'sleet', 67: 'sleet',\n91:   71: 'snow', 73: 'snow', 75: 'snow', 77: 'snow',\n92:   80: 'rain', 81: 'rain', 82: 'heavy-rain',\n93:   85: 'snow', 86: 'snow',\n94:   95: 'thunderstorm', 96: 'thunderstorm', 99: 'thunderstorm',\n95: };\n96: \n97: /** Chinese labels for WMO codes (used by the Shanghai card). */\n98: const WMO_ZH = {\n99:   0: '晴', 1: '晴', 2: '少云', 3: '多云', 45: '雾', 48: '雾',\n100:   51: '毛毛雨', 53: '毛毛雨', 55: '毛毛雨', 56: '冻雨', 57: '冻雨',\n101:   61: '小雨', 63: '中雨', 65: '大雨', 66: '冻雨', 67: '冻雨',\n102:   71: '小雪', 73: '中雪', 75: '大雪', 77: '雪粒',\n103:   80: '阵雨', 81: '中阵雨', 82: '大雨', 85: '小雪花', 86: '大雪花',\n104:   95: '雷暴', 96: '雷暴', 99: '雷暴',\n105: };\n106: \n107: function codeToCondition(code) {\n108:   const key = WMO_CODE_MAP[code];\n109:   return key && ICONS[key] ? { code: key, ...ICONS[key] } : null;\n110: }\n111: \n112: function round1(n) {\n113:   return Math.round(n * 10) / 10;\n114: }\n115: \n116: function extractTime(observedAt) {\n117:   const m = String(observedAt ?? '').match(/T(\\d{2}:\\d{2})/);\n118:   return m ? m[1] : null;\n119: }\n120: \n121: const WEEKDAY_ZH = ['一', '二', '三', '四', '五', '六', '日'];\n122: \n123: function weekdayOf(dateStr) {\n124:   const m = /^(\\d{4})-(\\d{2})-(\\d{2})$/.exec(String(dateStr ?? ''));\n125:   if (!m) return '';\n126:   return WEEKDAY_ZH[new Date(Number(m[1]), Number(m[2]) - 1, Number(m[3])).getDay()];\n127: }\n128:   return String(v ?? '').replace(/[&<>\"']/g, (ch) => ({\n129:     '&': '&amp;', '<': '&lt;', '>': '&gt;', '\"': '&quot;', \"'\": '&#39;'\n130:   }[ch]));\n131: }\n132: \n133: export function unitOf(city) {\n134:   const u = String(city.unit ?? city.tempUnit ?? 'C').replace(/°/g, '').toUpperCase();\n135:   return u === 'F' ? '°F' : '°C';\n136: }\n137: \n138: export function resolveCondition(city) {\n139:   const raw = String(\n140:     city.condition ?? city.icon ?? city.weather?.condition ?? city.weather?.icon ?? 'clear'\n141:   ).toLowerCase().replace(/\\s+/g, '-');\n142:   if (ICONS[raw]) return { code: raw, ...ICONS[raw] };\n143:   for (const rule of KEYWORD_RULES) {\n144:     if (rule.re.test(raw)) return { code: rule.name.code, ...rule.name };\n145:   }\n146:   return { code: 'cloudy', ...FALLBACK };\n147: }\n148: \n149: function themeFor(code) {\n150:   const light = LIGHT.includes(code);\n151:   return {\n152:     text: light ? '#1a202c' : '#f7fafc',\n153:     chip: light ? 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.30)' : 'rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14)',\n154:   };\n155: }\n156: \n157: function statRows(city) {\n158:   const rows = [\n159:     { label: 'Feels like', value: city.feelsLike != null ? `${esc(city.feelsLike)}${unitOf(city)}` : null },\n160:     { label: 'Humidity',   value: city.humidity   != null ? `${esc(city.humidity)}%` : null },\n161:     { label: 'Wind',       value: city.windKmh    != null\n162:       ? `${esc(city.windKmh)} km/h${city.windDirection ? ' ' + esc(city.windDirection) : ''}`\n163:       : null },\n164:     { label: 'Today',      value: city.high != null && city.low != null\n165:       ? `${esc(city.high)}° / ${esc(city.low)}°` : null },\n166:   ];\n167:   return rows\n168:     .filter((r) => r.value != null)\n169:     .map((r) => `<div class=\"wc-stat\"><span class=\"wc-stat-label\">${r.label}</span><span class=\"wc-stat-value\">${r.value}</span></div>`)\n170:     .join('');\n171: }\n172: \n173: function hourlyRow(hourly, unit) {\n174:   if (!Array.isArray(hourly) || hourly.length === 0) return '';\n175:   const items = hourly\n176:     .map((h) => {\n177:       const cond = resolveCondition(h);\n178:       const t = h.temp != null ? `${esc(h.temp)}${unit}` : '';\n179:       return `<div class=\"wc-hour\"><span class=\"wc-hour-time\">${esc(h.time ?? '')}</span><span class=\"wc-hour-icon\" aria-hidden=\"true\">${cond.emoji}</span><span class=\"wc-hour-temp\">${t}</span></div>`;\n180:     })\n181:     .join('');\n182:   return `<div class=\"wc-hourly\" aria-label=\"Hourly forecast\">${items}</div>`;\n183: }\n184: \n185: export function renderWeatherCard(city) {\n186:   const unit = unitOf(city);\n187:   const cond = resolveCondition(city);\n188:   const label = esc(city.description ?? cond.label);\n189:   const theme = themeFor(cond.code);\n190:   const gradient = GRADIENTS[cond.code] ?? GRADIENTS.cloudy;\n191: \n192:   const sub = city.country != null\n193:     ? `<span class=\"wc-sub\">${esc(city.country)}</span>`\n194:     : '';\n195:   const time = city.time != null ? `<span class=\"wc-time\">${esc(city.time)}</span>` : '';\n196: \n197:   const header = `<div class=\"wc-header\"><div class=\"wc-location\"><span class=\"wc-city\">${esc(city.city)}</span>${sub